Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: enable THP for GEM buffers

More than 2x speedup on darktable benchmark which was bottlenecked on page
allocation/pinning.

BACKPORT from the freedreno list, "[PATCH 1/2] drm/msm: Enable THP for GEM
buffers", Rob Clark, 2026-09-03:
https://www.mail-archive.com/freedreno@lists.freedesktop.org/msg46777.html

The core plumbing (drm_gem_huge_mnt_create(), dev->huge_mnt and the
shmem_file_setup_with_mnt() path in drm_gem_object_init()) is already in
the pinned 7.2.3 -- only the msm side is missing, so this is small.

"within_size" only allocates a huge page when it falls fully within the GEM
object's size, so it does not inflate small buffers.  Failure is not fatal:
without the mount, drm_gem_object_init() just falls back to the default
shmem mount, so we log it and carry on rather than failing probe over a
performance optimisation.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(separate_gpu_drm, "Use separate DRM device for the GPU (0=single DRM device for both GPU and display (default), 1=two DRM devices)");
 module_param(separate_gpu_kms, bool, 0400);
 
+static bool transparent_hugepage = true;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(transparent_hugepage, "Use transparent hugepages for GEM buffers");
+module_param(transparent_hugepage, bool, 0400);
+
 DECLARE_FAULT_ATTR(fail_gem_alloc);
 DECLARE_FAULT_ATTR(fail_gem_iova);
 
@@ -148,6 +152,12 @@
 	}
 
 	dma_set_max_seg_size(dev, UINT_MAX);
+
+	if (transparent_hugepage) {
+		ret = drm_gem_huge_mnt_create(ddev, "within_size");
+		if (ret)
+			DRM_DEV_INFO(dev, "no THP for GEM buffers: %d\n", ret);
+	}
 
 	/* Bind all our sub-components: */
 	if (gpu_ops)
